source_proof = "The module asserts README source facts and follows documented producer, transport and consumer source connections: node host and consensus source, transaction acceptance/forwarding, durable receipt release, root-path JSON-RPC dispatch, receipt rungs and committed coverage, authenticated commitment guidance and retired executor gates. It parses the documented curl arguments and JSON payload, the numbered transaction flow and node/library build commands, checks Makefile prerequisites and output, and resolves operator navigation links. It asserts the inclusive api1..api14 root-host range, chain 125/0x7d and absence of separate daemon/deployment guidance."
review_only = "Native Go/C/Rust builds, shell command execution, actual node startup, transaction execution, signature validation, WAL restart/recovery, public endpoint availability and BFT commitment are not executed by this gate. Source assertions prove documentation consistency rather than runtime certification. This doc-drift finding changes no interface or stateful component, so no restart or interface behavior proof is claimed. No shell scripts, unit files, manifests or build files are changed. Tests require only Python and pytest, with no external binary, subprocess, credential, environment variable, endpoint, native artifact or device."
